      "id": "2a26j1t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Prime Minister and Council of Ministers"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Prime Minister is appointed by the President of India under Article 75 of the Constitution.",
        "The Prime Minister can be a member of either the Lok Sabha or the Rajya Sabha.",
        "The Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to the Lok Sabha (Article 75).",
        "The Council of Ministers consists of three categories: Cabinet Ministers, Ministers of State, and Deputy Ministers.",
        "Article 78 lays down the duties of the Prime Minister regarding furnishing administrative information to the President."
      ],
      "id": "76zuv3x"
    },
